<title>GERMANY: DASA details 1996 sales.</title>
<headline>DASA details 1996 sales.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Provisional results for full-year 1996. (Figures in billions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>					    1996		1995</p>
<p>    Group sales			 13.0     vs     11.5</p>
<p>    Group incoming orders	   16.9     vs     10.9</p>
<p>    Group workforce (year-end)  44,936     vs   46,892</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures have been calculated to the U.S. GAAP accounting standard. They strip out from 1995 the contribution made by companies which were disposed of in 1996, including Fokker N.V. and Dornier Luftfarht.</p>
<p>DASA's 1995 annual report said group sales were 15.0 billion marks.</p>
<p>The company gave the following divisional breakdown.</p>
<p>					    1996		1995</p>
<p>Propulsions systems</p>
<p>    Sales				  2.3     vs	1.7</p>
<p>    Incoming orders		    2.1     vs	1.6</p>
<p>    Workforce			  6,281     vs    6,729</p>
<p>Aircraft</p>
<p>    Sales				  6.0     vs	5.3</p>
<p>    Incoming orders		    8.8     vs	5.3</p>
<p>    Workforce			 25,483     vs   26,807</p>
<p>Space systems</p>
<p>    Sales				  2.1     vs	1.9</p>
<p>    Incoming orders		    3.6     vs	2.0</p>
<p>    Workforce			  3,428     vs    3,417</p>
<p>Defence and civil systems</p>
<p>    Sales				  2.6     vs	2.7</p>
<p>    Incoming orders		    2.4     vs	2.0</p>
<p>    Workforce			  8,906     vs    9,042</p>
<p>NOTE - DASA is a unit of Daimler-Benz AG.</p>
</text>
